'''Mike McDonald''' (born June 22, 1958) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[long snapper]] for nine seasons in the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref name="mcdonald1">Lowery, Steve (25 September 1986). [https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1986-09-25-sp-9746-story.html Mike McDonald's Back in a Snap : He Rejoins the Rams as Center for Punts and Kicks], ''[[Los Angeles Times]]''</ref><ref name="lions1">(17 December 1992). [https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=1350&dat=19921217&id=DSgxAAAAIBAJ&sjid=igMEAAAAIBAJ&pg=6576,5330295&hl=en Lions sign two centers to fill gaps], ''Toledo Blade''</ref><ref name="snappers">Dufresne, Chris (4 August 1989). [https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1989-08-04-sp-655-story.html l LIFE'S A SNAP : McDonald, 31, Has Made Himself a Mini-Career With Rams as Long-Snapper], ''[[Los Angeles Times]]''</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[USC Trojans football|USC Trojans]].

He was first added to the roster of the [[Los Angeles Rams]] in late 1983, over three years after he had graduated from the [[University of Southern California]], to fill in for the injured [[Doug Barnett]].<ref name="signed">(29 December 1983). [https://www.nytimes.com/1983/12/29/sports/scouting-143208.html New Ram Reaps Playoff Benefits], ''[[The New York Times]]''</ref>

